# Cache policy for the files that are not content-hashed.
#
# Cloudflare's asset layer defaults every unhashed file to
# `public, max-age=0, must-revalidate`. Nothing on this site was edge-cacheable
# except /_app/immutable/, so the edge re-read whole objects on every hit. The
# prerendered /map document alone is 3.7 MB, and it was the single largest
# source of sustained 504s.
#
# The SvelteKit Cloudflare adapter appends its own block to this file at build
# time. That block owns /_app/ and /_app/immutable/, so those paths are absent
# here. A more specific rule has to unset Cache-Control before setting it,
# otherwise the value from /* is merged with it.

/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, s-maxage=60

# Documents are deliberately held for one minute and no longer. A deploy
# replaces the hashed bundles that the HTML references, so serving a stale
# document for hours would point browsers at chunks that no longer exist.
# Sixty seconds is enough to collapse a request flood into one origin read.

/tiles/*
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400, stale-while-revalidate=604800

/images/*
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400, stale-while-revalidate=604800

/icons/*
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800
